# Agent Orchestration

The Cursor main Agent is the QuantaHub Master/Orchestrator. Do not create an extra orchestration subagent.

## Mandatory routing table

Invoke specialists automatically using these triggers:

### quanta-platform — REQUIRED when work touches
- CTFd core integration, plugins, themes or APIs,
- authentication/identity,
- users, teams, challenges or flags,
- learning/progress/organizations/tenancy,
- platform-side relational models or migrations,
- platform API behavior.

### quanta-lab-engine — REQUIRED when work touches
- Lab Registry or Lab Manifest,
- sessions or lifecycle,
- scheduler/capacity,
- runner agents,
- Docker/gVisor/Firecracker/KVM runtime providers,
- TTL/reset/cleanup/orphan reconciliation,
- Lab Gateway routing/resource profiles.

### quanta-frontend — REQUIRED when work touches
- dashboard,
- learning paths/rooms,
- CTFd theme UI,
- lab start/stop/reset controls,
- terminal/web embedding,
- responsive/accessibility behavior.

### quanta-security — REQUIRED review when work touches
- authentication/authorization/tenant isolation,
- secrets or service identity,
- lab/runtime privilege,
- networking/DNS/ingress/egress,
- browser origins/domains/cookies,
- gateways,
- supply chain,
- malware/high-risk labs,
- abuse controls,
- administrative security.

### quanta-verifier — REQUIRED after every meaningful implementation
Meaningful includes any behavior, contract, schema, migration, security, lab runtime, API, UI flow or infrastructure change.

## Multi-domain tasks

If a task touches multiple ownership domains:
1. invoke every required implementation specialist,
2. run independent work in parallel only when file/ownership overlap is absent,
3. integrate results through the main Agent,
4. run quanta-security if any security trigger exists,
5. run quanta-verifier last.

## No delegation questions

Do not ask the user which specialist to use. This table decides.

Repository rules/docs are canonical memory; chat history is not.
